    "d2B-AU-1Gk.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"Tobacco comes from the leaves of the Nicotiana plant and is used in things like cigarettes, cigars, and chewing tobacco. The main thing in tobacco is nicotine, a natural substance that can be addictive and affect your brain\\n\\nWhen people smoke cigarettes, they inhale over 7,000 chemicals, and nicotine is the one that makes smoking addictive. There are also other chemicals added to make the smoke taste better and for the nicotine to be absorbed more easily.\\n\\nEach time someone smokes a cigarette, they get about 1-2 milligrams of nicotine, which quickly goes to their brain and makes their heart beat faster, raises their blood pressure, and increases their breathing. It's kind of like a quick energy boost, but it can become a habit.\\n\\nCigarettes are designed so that someone who smokes regularly gets around 200 \\\"hits\\\" of nicotine to their brain every day. Other tobacco products, like chewing tobacco, also have nicotine. Some people use e-cigarettes to get nicotine without all the extra chemicals in tobacco smoke.\\n\\nNicotine works on the brain in a way that makes it feel good and can become a habit because it gives a sense of pleasure. That's why it's important to understand what's in tobacco and the effects it can have on your body and brain.\\n\"; ObjectID = \"d2B-AU-1Gk\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Tobacco comes from the leaves of the Nicotiana plant and is used in things like cigarettes, cigars, and chewing tobacco. The main thing in tobacco is nicotine, a natural substance that can be addictive and affect your brain\n\nWhen people smoke cigarettes, they inhale over 7,000 chemicals, and nicotine is the one that makes smoking addictive. There are also other chemicals added to make the smoke taste better and for the nicotine to be absorbed more easily.\n\nEach time someone smokes a cigarette, they get about 1-2 milligrams of nicotine, which quickly goes to their brain and makes their heart beat faster, raises their blood pressure, and increases their breathing. It's kind of like a quick energy boost, but it can become a habit.\n\nCigarettes are designed so that someone who smokes regularly gets around 200 \"hits\" of nicotine to their brain every day. Other tobacco products, like chewing tobacco, also have nicotine. Some people use e-cigarettes to get nicotine without all the extra chemicals in tobacco smoke.\n\nNicotine works on the brain in a way that makes it feel good and can become a habit because it gives a sense of pleasure. That's why it's important to understand what's in tobacco and the effects it can have on your body and brain.\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
